        ⚠ THE <inlineHelpText> BELOW WAS AT 247 OF ITS 255-CHARACTER CAP AS OF 2026-08-14, AND IT
        ENUMERATES EVERY VALUE. SEE THE 2026-08-21 MASTER RETRACTION BELOW FOR THE CURRENT COUNT.
        ================================================================================
        MEASURED 2026-08-14 with System.Xml.XmlDocument.Load() on the DECODED stored value, not
        with a grep - a Get-Content -Raw read mangles the non-ASCII characters this repo's files
        are full of and reports the wrong number. 247/255 leaves EIGHT characters, and this help
        text is written as two full enumerations (five acquisition values, then five disposition
        values). A new value costs ", " plus its own label, so ANY name longer than six
        characters breaches on the day it is added - and 'Under Review', the shortest value this
        phase introduced anywhere, is twelve.

        🔴 IT IS NOT A DEFECT TODAY. It is recorded because it is the SAME ELEMENT CLASS this
        phase already breached TWICE - RecordType.description earlier, and this object's sibling
        Is_Advance_Allowed__c.inlineHelpText (fixed to 241/255, see that file). Both were caught
        only by measuring, never by review, and both were introduced by an edit that looked like
        prose.

        ⇒ WHEN IT BREACHES, DO NOT TRIM A VALUE OUT OF THE LIST to buy room - a help text that
        enumerates SOME of the choices is worse than one that enumerates none, because the
        omission reads as "not available on your record type". Drop BOTH enumerations and say
        the choices differ by record type, which is the only part a user acts on. The full lists
        already live in <description> above and in the two record type files, neither of which
        is capped the same way (CustomField.description is 1000).

