        FILE RATHER THAN TRUSTING THIS SENTENCE.
        =====================================================================================

        WHAT ACTUALLY MOVED: the Disposition_LOI record type's inclusion list (a different file -
        objects/LOI__c/recordTypes/Disposition_LOI.recordType-meta.xml). 'Countered by DPEG',
        'Counter Received from Buyer' and 'Executed' are REMOVED from that record type;
        'Negotiation' and 'Signed' - both ALREADY on this master field since 2026-08-14, added for
        Acquisition_LOI - are now ALSO included on Disposition_LOI. Every value this record type
        needs already existed here; this pass needed no append, no insert, and no interleave -
        the arithmetic that made prior LOI__c value additions load-bearing does not apply to this
        change at all, because nothing was added to the FIELD.

        NEW RENDERING, RE-DERIVED FROM THE UNCHANGED MASTER ORDER:
          Disposition_LOI -> Received(6), Under Review(7), Negotiation(12), Signed(13)
        Still strictly monotonic (6 &lt; 7 &lt; 12 &lt; 13), so this record type's new four-step
        Path renders correctly with the master order exactly as it already stood. Acquisition_LOI
        is unaffected: Draft(1), Under Review(7), Submitted(11), Negotiation(12), Signed(13),
        byte-identical to before this change.

        🔴 BOTH TERMINALS ARE NOW 'Signed'. The "terminals stay distinct" property this file
        relied on twice above (the non-terminal-overlap paragraph and the PSA-analogy section) is
        gone. The one terminal-state test on this object, Is_Advance_Allowed__c's
        `TEXT(Stage__c) &lt;&gt; "Signed"` clause, SURVIVES this without any edit, because that
        clause was already record-type-agnostic - it excludes 'Signed' on EITHER record type,
        which is now correct for both rather than correct for one and coincidentally inert for
        the other. See that field's own header for the full analysis of why its
        `&lt;&gt; "Executed"` clause is RETAINED - not as dead code, but as a narrow, still-live
        guard against one specific degenerate shape: a Master-record-type row. 'Executed' sits on
        no record type as of this change, so the clause is inert for both Acquisition_LOI and
        Disposition_LOI rows, but a Master-typed LOI is not constrained by either record type's
        picklistValues allow-list and can still be saved at Stage__c = 'Executed' by a data load,
        a direct Apex write, or a record-type-less TestDataFactory fixture - for that population
        the clause is the only thing hiding Advance Stage at a stage with no legitimate next
        step. Code review adjudicated this reading as correct (S2, 2026-08-21); do not describe
        the clause as dead code.

        🔴 'Countered by DPEG', 'Counter Received from Buyer' AND 'Executed' STAY ACTIVE ON THIS
        FIELD, PERMANENTLY, FOR NOW - ORPHANED, NOT DEACTIVATED. They sit on NO record type as of
        this change (Acquisition_LOI never carried them; Disposition_LOI just stopped). Consistent
