    <description>Lifecycle state of the LOI. THE MASTER SET IS THE UNION OF TWO RECORD-TYPE SETS AND NO SINGLE RECORD TYPE SEES ALL THIRTEEN. Acquisition_LOI runs Draft, Under Review, Submitted, Negotiation, Signed. Disposition_LOI runs Received, Under Review, Negotiation, Signed (narrowed 2026-08-21; was Received, Under Review, Countered by DPEG, Counter Received from Buyer, Executed). THE TWO SETS NOW OVERLAP AT THREE VALUES - Under Review, Negotiation, Signed - AND BOTH TERMINALS ARE NOW Signed, so this field alone does NOT identify the record type; the discriminator is the parent lookup or the per-record-type allow-list, never the value alone. Countered by DPEG, Counter Received from Buyer and Executed stay ACTIVE though on no record type. Prepare/Review, Sent, Counter and Completed are retired acquisition values, inactive after the Phase 3 migration, never deleted. Drives LOI_Path_Acquisition / LOI_Path_Disposition and RecordStageAdvanceService.</description>
